  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🐺 Minecraft Pet Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Name tag ideas for every Minecraft pet, from wolves and cats to axolotls and allays."
    },
    "intro": "This **Minecraft pet name generator** has name tag ideas for wolves, cats, horses, parrots, axolotls, foxes, llamas, camels, frogs and allays, in cute, cool, funny and food styles. A name tag keeps your pets from despawning and makes them easier to find, and a good name makes them family.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How to name a pet in Minecraft",
        "content": "<p>To name a pet in Minecraft, tame it, rename a name tag on an anvil, then use the name tag on the pet.</p><ul><li><strong>Taming first:</strong> wolves are tamed with bones, cats with raw fish, parrots with seeds, and horses and llamas by riding them until they stop throwing you off. Camels don't need taming: just put a saddle on. Axolotls and frogs can't be tamed, but you can carry axolotls in a bucket and name them.</li><li><strong>Naming:</strong> rename a name tag on an anvil (one level of experience), then use it on the pet. Named mobs don't despawn, and the name makes it easier to find in a crowd of cats.</li><li><strong>Allays</strong> will follow you once you give them an item, so they deserve a name too.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Secret Minecraft name tag names",
        "content": "<p>Some names change how a mob looks or behaves when you put them on a name tag.</p><p>A few names do something special when you use them on a mob (most of these are Java Edition):</p><ul><li><strong>Dinnerbone</strong> or <strong>Grumm:</strong> the mob turns upside down.</li><li><strong>jeb_:</strong> a sheep cycles through every colour of the rainbow.</li><li><strong>Toast:</strong> a rabbit gets a special coat.</li><li><strong>Johnny:</strong> a vindicator attacks almost every mob it sees, so keep it away from your pets.</li></ul><p>And the pink axolotl is called <em>lucy</em> in the game's files. For your villagers, try the <a href=\"minecraft-villager-name-generator.html\">Minecraft Villager Name Generator</a>.</p><p>For everything else in Minecraft, see all the <a href=\"../categories/minecraft-names.html\">Minecraft name generators</a>.</p><p>More for your Minecraft world: <a href=\"minecraft-username-generator.html\">usernames</a> and <a href=\"minecraft-world-name-generator.html\">world names</a>.</p><p>For a black cat at Halloween, try the <a href=\"black-cat-name-generator.html\">Black Cat Name Generator</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What should I name my Minecraft dog?",
        "answer": "Choose Wolf: cute names like Biscuit, cool ones like Ranger, or funny ones like Not a Creeper."
      },
      {
        "question": "What is the pink axolotl called in Minecraft?",
        "answer": "In the game's files the pink (leucistic) axolotl is called lucy. The others are wild, gold, cyan and the rare blue."
      },
      {
        "question": "What happens if you name a mob Dinnerbone?",
        "answer": "It turns upside down. Grumm does the same."
      },
      {
        "question": "Do name tags stop mobs despawning?",
        "answer": "Yes. Any mob with a name from a name tag won't despawn."
      },
      {
        "question": "What are good Minecraft cat names?",
        "answer": "Choose Cat for names like Pepper, Mittens or Sir Pounce. Cats in Minecraft are tamed with raw cod or salmon."
      },
      {
        "question": "What are good Minecraft horse names?",
        "answer": "Choose Horse for names like Thunder, Clover or Sir Gallops. Horses are tamed by riding them until they stop throwing you off."
      }
    ]
  },
  "seoTitle": "Minecraft Pet Names: Dog, Cat, Horse & Axolotl Ideas"
